QECops, by Jithesh Mithra. MIT licensed. doi:10.5281/zenodo.19410365,
https://github.com/JitheshMithra/QECops

  Two things in this package derive from QECops:

    syndrome_leakage/hardware.py   the Shor [[9,1,3]] syndrome-extraction circuit
                                   layout used by build_shor_circuits, ported to
                                   this package's generator order. The state
                                   preparation differs: QECops encodes |0> and |1>,
                                   which are |+_L> and |-_L> in this package's
                                   logical basis, so build_shor_circuits feeds
                                   |+> and |-> instead to prepare |0_L> and |1_L>.

    syndrome_leakage/channels.py   the quenched per-qubit noise model, a product
                                   channel with a different damping strength on
                                   each qubit, which the `disorder` run uses.

